  {
    "sha": "9351f22ec629136a85dc073b29947ced3afc1c4d",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDkzNTFmMjJlYzYyOTEzNmE4NWRjMDczYjI5OTQ3Y2VkM2FmYzFjNGQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T23:47:53Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T23:47:53Z"
      },
      "message": "refactor(sim): move FieldPlay and PlayWorker from app to the simulation crate\n\nFieldPlay, PlayIndex, PlayWorker, the playhead, the cut dispatch, the\nlayer mode, the precalc bindings and the packed frame move to\ncamcraft-sim (play*.rs, play_worker*.rs). The plain-data parts they read\nmove with them: FieldView and its packed lattice and display-field build\n(camcraft_sim::field_view), the rotary slice cut and its pose tolerance,\nand LathePlan (camcraft_sim::stock_sim).\n\nApp keeps the world reads and re-exports each moved item at its old\npath. PlaySeed is an app newtype over the sim's PlayInputs, and\nPlaySeed::gather converts each planned op. FieldPlay::new/with_budget\nbecome the app trait FieldPlayWorld. The worker takes the host clock\nfrom PlayInputs (app passes clock::monotonic, the #31 wasm32 seam), so\ncamcraft-sim gets no new dependency.\n\nPinned by play::tests (camcraft-sim lib): the playback built and driven\nfrom plain inputs with no world.\n\nFixes #2268\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
